Package: classir
Title: Tools for Preparing and Analysing Psychological Data
Version: 0.0.0.9008
Authors@R: 
    person("David", "Sidhu", 
           email = "david.sidhu@carleton.ca", 
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Functions for the typical kinds of operations psychologists (and
    other researchers) do in R, including surveying datasets ('look'),
    preparing them for analysis ('prep') and combining them ('add_values').
    Also includes functions geared towards psycholinguistic analyses but
    potentially useful more widely: simplifying the random effects structure
    of a linear mixed effects model until it converges ('converge'), running
    several approaches to building a regression model and reporting all of
    the results together ('compare_methods'), and transcribing words into
    IPA ('transcribe_phonemes').
